[{"tag_name":"v271","created_at":"2026-11-08T05:16:44Z","body":"\nThis release includes a some nice contributions form the community:\n\n- @cphlipot improved the sidebar on mobile\n- @candrews added model parsing from the websocket stream in v1/realtime\n- @heshiming added support for TensorFold metrics parsing\n\nOn the backend there was lots of work to finetune LFM3-1.7B for\nthe new help agent on llama-swap.ai. This includes the training scripts\nand data and the new docbot package that has the Help's mcp endpoints.\n\n\n- [PR #1283](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1283) ui: dismiss mobile sidebar when user selects an item: closes the mobile sidebar overlay as soon as a nav item is tapped so the selected page comes into focus immediately, because the overlay previously stayed open and made switching pages (eg. activity -> playground) take two taps; no effect on desktop where the sidebar is always visible by [@cphlipot](https://github.com/cphlipot)\n- [PR #1304](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1304) evals/docs-agent: update cases for current KB and tune the Docs Agent: adds 66 training and 29 holdout eval cases, fixes four wrong assertions, raises `get_doc` default output from 250 to 400 lines (it was cutting off the kubeswap gpu-budget example), corrects the cmdStop, `${PORT}` macro and kubeswap docs, and points KB pages at the guides holding the answers, lifting gemma-4-12B-r9700's training score from 96.0% to 97.3% by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1308](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1308) evals/docs-agent: add fine-tuning pipeline for a small Docs Agent model: adds the scripts, recorded conversations and run notes used to fine-tune LFM3-1.7B on Docs Agent conversations (lfm3-v2 Q4_K_M scores 95.5% on training cases and 96.1% on the holdout at a 60 s per-question limit), with no weights included, as a reference for tuning future help-agent models by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1310](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1310) internal/server: route /v1/realtime by model in session.update: fixes 404s before the websocket upgrade for clients that follow OpenAI's documented `/v1/realtime` API and connect with `?intent=transcription` but no `?model=`, by having llama-swap complete the handshake itself, buffer events until a `session.update` names a model (`session.model`, then the transcription model keys), and replay them upstream through the normal model chain, reporting failures as OpenAI style error events by [@candrews](https://github.com/candrews)\n- [PR #1312](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1312) docbot: new importable package: extracts MCP protocol handling into a stateless `internal/mcpserver.Handler` and adds a `docbot` package that serves llama-swap's docs (and optionally source) as MCP tools over any HTTP route with `SystemPrompt()` and `Tools()` helpers, a prerequisite for the help agent on llama-swap.ai by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1313](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1313) TensorFold support for pluggable usage handlers: adds a TensorFold usage and metrics extractor with simplified captured-metrics fixtures, rebuilt on the pluggable per-upstream usage handler standard from #1292 after that refactor left the original TensorFold support stale by [@heshiming](https://github.com/heshiming)\n- [dea1363](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/commit/dea136356a896a2d65e5085f515297e8a17368bd) README.md: add tip for llama-swap.ai: adds a README tip pointing to the browser-based Chat agent powered by an LFM3-1.7B fine tuned on the docs by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [cef61b3](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/commit/cef61b366385e8fbcaec2c02d3beca3469ea31ed) Revise Chat agent info in README: revises the Chat agent description and links to the fine-tuned model on Hugging Face by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [c805e62](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/commit/c805e6281071caf4540ae6490d7cca076ebf263c) Update link format for Chat agent in README: links the whole \"Chat agent on llama-swap.ai\" phrase to the chat docs page by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v270","created_at":"2026-11-05T03:41:09Z","body":"\nOhh, support for the v1/realtime API with LFM3 voice chat in the Playground!\nThe Help agent has been updated with a guide on how to quickly get it set up\nand working.\n\nAlso in this release are a few compatbility and quality improvements.\nThanks to @noctrex, @SriRamanujam, and @ltjax for the contributions.\n\n- [PR #1278](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1278) Feat/sidebar category submenus: adds category submenus to the left sidebar menu, mirroring the capability-derived categories recently added to the Models list by [@noctrex](https://github.com/noctrex) and [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1288](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1288) Configurable token rate sources: adds hints, docs and usage extraction for hipfire so token/s stats are captured correctly when running hipfire behind llama-swap, as part of the pluggable per-upstream usage parsing by [@ltjax](https://github.com/ltjax)\n- [PR #1291](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1291) cmd/kubeswap: Support defining annotations and service accounts: allows defining annotations on generated deployments and pods (rejecting the reserved `kubeswap.io/model-id` key) and setting `.spec.template.spec.serviceAccountName` on the Deployment, without managing the ServiceAccount itself by [@SriRamanujam](https://github.com/SriRamanujam)\n- [PR #1297](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1297) fix(logmon): stop memory accumulating across config reloads: closes a process's dedicated log monitor when `ProcessCommand.run` returns so discarded router generations no longer leak memory, because each monitor's surviving broadcast goroutine kept its 100 KiB history buffer reachable after a hot reload (129 MiB retained after 100 router replacements in testing, now ~0) by [@junmo-kim](https://github.com/junmo-kim)\n- [PR #1298](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1298) makefile: use .stamp for UI dependency checks: uses a `.stamp` file to detect UI dependency changes, fixing a build error after pulling the latest version when UI dependencies changed by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1299](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1299) internal/server: add /v1/realtime proxying and a Realtime playground: proxies OpenAI Realtime API style websockets to the upstream named by the `?model=` query and adds a Playground > Realtime tab for speech-to-speech models like LFM3 Audio through llama-server (push-to-talk or hands-free voice detection, streamed playback, replay/download per turn), records each session as one Activity row with reply, token, decode-rate and audio-second metrics, detects audio output from `/v1/models` `output_modalities`, and adds a KB guide with llama-server configuration examples by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v269","created_at":"2026-11-01T00:57:44Z","body":"\nHappy Halloween!\n\nLots of small and big treats in this release.\n\n- captures can now be persisted to disk and not lost on restart.\n- the metrics capture backend has been refactored to make it easy\n  to add support for new inference servers.\n- the UI can show models sorted by categories, great if you have\n  many different types configured!  \n- metrics can be exported as a PNG to make sharing easier.\n- add support for the embedding model capability\n- small bug and UI improvements\n\nDetails below:\n\n- [PR #1274](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1274) go.mod,ui/package-lock.json: dependency updates: picks up security updates for node and moves `shirou/gopsutil` back to the main upstream repository by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1275](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1275) feat(config): add embeddings capability flag: adds `capabilities.embeddings`, mirroring the existing `reranker` flag and rendered into the `/v1/models` capabilities map, because capability discovery reads llama-server `/props` which reports nothing about embeddings, so a probed embed model surfaced as plain text->text and clients and the UI could only pick them out by name prefix by [@noctrex](https://github.com/noctrex)\n- [PR #1276](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1276) feat(ui): group Models list into capability-derived class sections: derives each model's class (Chat, Image, Video, Audio, Embeddings, Rerank) client-side from the capability flags and modality lists `/v1/models` already carries and renders one collapsible section per class with a status dot that aggregates its rows, because a long flat list is hard to scan once many models are configured; `/api/events` modelStatus now includes `modalities: {in, out}` from the same `renderCapabilities` call so the dashboard and the OpenAI listing cannot disagree by [@noctrex](https://github.com/noctrex)\n- [PR #1279](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1279) ui: move Models display options into a dropdown menu: moves the Categories and Show unlisted models switches into a \"Display options\" menu pinned to the right of the Models header (with the unlisted count shown in the item) and drops `flex-wrap`, because the header added in #1276 wrapped onto extra rows and made the page too tall; mobile layout improved too by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1280](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1280) Makefile: add native target for the host platform: makes `native` the default target so a bare `make` builds for the platform you are on instead of cross-compiling everything, and fixes `make all` to actually cover Windows and FreeBSD, with `$(LDFLAGS)` factored out and shared by every platform target by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1282](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1282) internal/capcompat: detect context length from yamz servers: reads `max_context` from `/v1/models` (tried after `context_length`) so yamz (kyojin) servers report their context length through the default prober by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1285](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1285) ui: export the activity table as a client-side PNG image: rasterizes the visible table in the browser with html-to-image (SVG foreignObject -> canvas) and adds Markdown / Screenshot tabs to the export dialog with clipboard copy, download and a background resolved from the nearest opaque ancestor, so exporting works without a new backend endpoint; Meta and Capture columns are excluded from the render (#1284) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1287](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1287) ui: make markdown code highlighting theme aware in light mode: drives highlight.js token colors from `--hljs-*` custom properties (with a per-theme `--link` color and a lighter `--muted` for Midnight Commander) instead of one globally imported dark-only stylesheet, because code was measured at 1.12-1.40:1 contrast and was effectively invisible in all 11 light themes; light-mode code contrast is now 10.76-13.35:1 with dark mode unchanged by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1290](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1290) internal/capcompat: read /props fields with gjson: extracts each `/props` field individually with gjson, so one unexpected field no longer takes the whole probe down, because llama-server b12017 added a list to `chat_template_caps` alongside its booleans which broke the whole-body unmarshal and made capability discovery fail against those builds; bad fields now log a WARN and read as their zero value (#1281) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1292](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1292) Extract usage parsing into pluggable upstream-specific handlers: splits usage extraction into per-upstream extractors (llama-server, vLLM, Anthropic, OpenAI, TabbyAPI, oMLX and an \"auto\" fallback that reads every known format) fed by the new `internal/hint` package which carries upstream and task information through the request context, and records task type, route, peer and reasoning tokens in the activity log, so token counts and performance metrics are accurate per upstream instead of assuming one format by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1293](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1293) ui: fix the Model page Logs panel scrolling the whole page: gives the page its own scroll container and a minimum height for the Activity/Logs tabs, so a long log scrolls inside the panel instead of pushing the whole page by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1294](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1294) Store request/response captures in separate SQLite database: moves captures out of the in-memory `internal/cache` into a capture repository backed by its own SQLite database (new `store.persistCaptures`, `captureBuffer` unchanged), so captures can persist across restarts without fragmenting the metrics db, are pruned asynchronously by compressed size and are addressed by a `yymmddhh-xxxx` capture id that activity rows link to; `internal/cache` is removed (#1115) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v268","created_at":"2026-10-28T03:25:51Z","body":"\nMany users run llama-swap on their gaming machines. The new Pause and Resume\nfunctionality unloads and pauses all inference, freeing up system resources for\nfun! Well llama-swap is fun too but you gotta be weird like me to prefer it\nover gaming.\n\nAlso a small change to the CUDA 13 container to support Turing architectures,\nwhere the actual cut off is.\n\n- [PR #1272](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1272) docker/unified: add compute capability 75 to cuda13 amd64 build: adds sm 75 to the default `CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES` for the amd64 `unified-cuda13` image, because it only compiled for sm 80 and up so Turing GPUs (Quadro T1000, RTX 20xx, GTX 16xx), which CUDA 13 still supports, failed at runtime with \"no kernel image is available for execution on the device\"; arm64 is unchanged (#1239) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [6c855da](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/commit/6c855da82bf7adb235bdf2e4abe9278aea703973) README: add turing architecture notes: lists Turing GPUs (RTX 20xx, GTX 16xx, Quadro T-series) as supported by the `unified-cuda13` image by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1273](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1273) server: add pause/resume inference: adds `/api/models/pause` and `/api/models/resume` endpoints and UI controls that unload all local models and reject new requests until resumed, so system resources can be freed while llama-swap keeps running (#1268) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v267","created_at":"2026-10-26T04:46:48Z","body":"\nThis is huge release with @JaredHatfield contributing a new capacity based router!\n\nRather than defining which models fit with other models, the capacity router\nallows declaring pools of resources and how much of each resource a model needs.\nThe new router will automatically evict models to free up enough capacity to\nload the new model. For use cases that have a big combinations of models\nthat can run concurrently, the new router can eliminate a lot of manual\nconfiguration work.\n\nThe other big feature is the Help Agent in the UI can now search llama-swap's\nsource code as well as its knowledge base. Every release of llama-swap includes\nthe source code it was built from (tests excluded). This is handy for answering\nquestions about how llama-swap actually works and a knowledge base article\ndoes not exist. One step closer to the singularity!\n\nIf you want to try out the new router ask the Help Agent to generate a configuration\nexample using your existing configuration. Did you know, it can do that!? :)\n\n\n- [PR #1242](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1242) router: add capacity-based model eviction: adds a capacity router where user-defined pools bound which models can be resident together and `evict_cost` picks what to unload when a model no longer fits, replacing the need to hand-maintain every valid combination in the matrix on systems with lots of unified memory (#1004) by [@JaredHatfield](https://github.com/JaredHatfield)\n- [PR #1258](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1258) docs/kb: add guides/tools for the cmd/ programs: adds knowledge base articles for wol-proxy, fake-model and vllm-wrapper (and moves the kubeswap guide under `guides/tools`) so the Help chat can answer questions about the tools in the llama-swap ecosystem, plus a convention for keeping each tool's README and article in sync by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1259](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1259) internal/mcptools: add code search to Help agent: gives the Docs agent `code__grep`, `code__read`, `code__find` and `code__ls` so it can verify knowledge base articles against the code that implements them, adds `helpagent.disable` to hide Help and stop serving `/api/mcp`, and raises the agent loop's max iterations from 16 to 96 so the extra tool calls do not end the answer early by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1265](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1265) internal/mcptools: embed source for code tools instead of git: embeds the Go and TypeScript source (without tests) in the binary via the new `embed_src` build tag and reads it through `fs.FS`, because the runtime `git` checkout made the code tools fail on installs without the git command line tool; `code__status` and `code__update` are removed by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v266","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:02:43Z","body":"\nThis release includes security dependency updates and requested quality of life changes from users:\n\n- the UI no longer expects to be run under a root path making it easier to serve llama-swap behind another proxy\n- the max request size is configurable now. Users should be free to OOM as much as they want. llama-swap ain't your mom!\n- allow manual override of values in /v1/audio/voices. This is a non-standard endpoint but makes working with upstream audio engines a bit nicer\n\nDetails below:\n\n- [PR #1224](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1224) cmd/kubeswap: attach DRA ResourceClaims and mount NFS volumes: add repeatable `--resource-claim` and NFS `--volume` support so Kubernetes backends can share a DRA GPU claim and mount models without a static PV and PVC for each export (#1222) by [@gabrielcosi](https://github.com/gabrielcosi)\n- [PR #1225](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1225) Add voices override for speech models: let local models configure `capabilities.voices` so `/v1/audio/voices` returns a reliable list without starting the model or querying the upstream server (#1207) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1228](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1228) ui,server: serve the UI under a reverse proxy base path: use relative asset, API and redirect paths so the UI works behind a prefix-stripping reverse proxy without routing its endpoints at the proxy root (#1227) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1249](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1249) internal/server: make the request body size limit configurable: add `maxRequestBodyMB` for model endpoints and Tailcat, replacing the fixed 250 MB cap while retaining 250 MB as the default (#1245) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1257](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1257) AGENTS.md, go.mod: use go 1.27.3, trim AGENT rules: raise the Go version to 1.27.3, update dependencies and simplify contributor instructions by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v265","created_at":"2026-10-14T08:29:38Z","body":"\nA couple of small improvements:\n\n- support serving llama-swap behind a path on a reverse proxy. Helpful if you want to front llama-swap with nginx and serve it under a specific path.\n- add support for manually defining voices for text to speech models\n- a small kubeswap update\n\n- [PR #1228](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1228) ui,server: serve the UI under a reverse proxy base path: makes the browser side base-path agnostic (relative asset, redirect, favicon and PWA URLs plus an `apiUrl()` helper that re-attaches a stripped prefix) so llama-swap works behind a plain prefix-stripping proxy at `https://host/subpath/llama-swap/` without routing `/ui`, `/api` and `/v1` at the proxy root; includes an nginx and Caddy guide (#1227) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1225](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1225) Add voices override for speech models: adds a `models.capabilities.voices` capability listing the voice ids an upstream server supports, because the non-standard `GET /v1/audio/voices` endpoint returns unreliable responses; falls back to probing that endpoint on a best-effort basis when the list is not set (#1207) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1224](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1224) cmd/kubeswap: attach DRA ResourceClaims and mount NFS volumes: adds a repeatable `--resource-claim name=claim` flag so backends can get GPUs via the NVIDIA DRA driver (kubeswap only references the claim, pods sharing a claim share its device) and an `nfs:server/export:path[:ro]` kind for `--volume` so models can be mounted from NFS without a static PV/PVC per export (#1222) by [@gabrielcosi](https://github.com/gabrielcosi)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v264","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:35:18Z","body":"This release includes a new `auto:orphans` set for swap matrix rules. This new set automatically includes all models that were not explictly added to a set.  It is defined as `(orphan1 | orphan2 | orphan3 | ...)`. The orphans set is handy for definitions like: `+always & +auto:orphans`, where `+always` is a set of models that are always loaded and should never be swapped out.\r\n\r\nThe /audiocpp endpoint was added to make working with audio.cpp server eaiser. The `audiocpp_auto` model is automatically used when the endpoint is requested. audio.cpp's OpenAI compatible endpoints can be accessed directly via `/audiocpp/v1/audio/*`. Very handy when used with llama-swap's unified docker container which builds audio.cpp with the UI and native model downloader.\r\n\r\nAlso one tiny commit to improve compatibility with llama-server's decision model functionality.\r\n\r\nThanks to the contributors in this release, especially @knguyen298 for being patient and keeping the PR updated.\r\n\r\n- [PR #1026](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1026) internal/matrix: add synthetic auto:orphans set: adds a `+auto:orphans` selector that expands to every model not named in another set, so a catch-all set like `\"+always & +auto:orphans\"` picks up new models automatically (#1025) by [@knguyen298](https://github.com/knguyen298)\r\n- [PR #1223](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1223) Add /audiocpp endpoint for audio.cpp UI passthrough: serves audio.cpp's web UI and model management through a dedicated `/audiocpp/` endpoint bound to the reserved `audiocpp_auto` model, like `/comfyui/`, so the unified container works without naming a model per request by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\r\n- [PR #1220](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1220) internal/capcompat: detect decision models from llama-server's listing: fix decision models being reported as `out: [text]` (and `capabilities.out: [decisions]` failing validation) because discovery only read `/props`; `output_modalities` from `/v1/models` is now used, and tools are only advertised when the model outputs text (#1219) by [@nazeshinjite](https://github.com/nazeshinjite)\r\n\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v263","created_at":"2026-10-10T06:16:39Z","body":"\nI've been busy, busy, busy and have not had as much time for llama-swap as I\nwould like. This release includes reliability improvements, improved\ncompatibility and some small quality of life improvements. Thank you for the\namazing contributors for this release! Everyone who files issues or submits a\nPR is greatly appreciated.\n\n- [PR #1213](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1213) Add confirmation UI and progress tracking for WoL wake: wol-proxy gets a `-require-confirm` flag that shows a \"Start server\" page instead of waking on every request, plus a retro loading page with a progress bar estimated from the last wake duration by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1215](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1215) internal/router: strip browser headers before proxying to peers: fix UI chats failing with a 401 against an api.anthropic.com peer, which treated the forwarded browser Origin header as a direct browser call; Origin, Referer, Sec-Fetch-* and Access-Control-Request-* are now removed (#1214) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1212](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1212) internal/process: report loading progress from the health check: parse `progress`/`message` from not-ready health check JSON bodies, show it on the Models and model detail pages, and restart the `healthCheckTimeout` countdown when progress changes so long loads don't time out (#1079, #1208) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1196](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1196) internal/perf: restart loop to trigger GPU collector when the monitor still running: fix GPU stats stopping for good after `nvidia-smi` exited; the exit error is now logged and the collector restarts with a 5 to 30 second backoff (#1155) by [@hpdkhoa](https://github.com/hpdkhoa)\n- [PR #1211](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1211) internal/process: add a per-model disableKeepAlives option (#1205): fix intermittent 502 `proxy error: EOF` when a POST reused a pooled connection that llama-server closed after a streamed response; `disableKeepAlives: true` opens a new connection per request by [@johnnieCR](https://github.com/johnnieCR)\n- [PR #1199](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1199) fix(metrics): show oMLX token rates in Activity: read oMLX's `usage.prompt_tokens_per_second` and `usage.generation_tokens_per_second` as a fallback so rates no longer show as unknown by [@junmo-kim](https://github.com/junmo-kim)\n- [PR #1198](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1198) internal/capcompat: add Gufo inference engine prober: add a default capability prober that uses only `/v1/models` data as the fallback for servers without a custom prober (vLLM, Gufo, SGLang, etc.), replacing the vLLM-specific one by [@berney](https://github.com/berney)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v262","created_at":"2026-10-03T06:28:28Z","body":"\nsystemone models are mega hyped right now. This release adds support for\n/v1/systemone for that fast thinking goodness(?). Also requests missing a\nContent-Type will get one automatically added for the inference endpoints.\n\n- [PR #1197](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1197) Add /v1/systemone endpoint to POST JSON routes: route llama.cpp's new /v1/systemone decision model endpoint to the model named in the JSON body (#1195) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1194](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1194) internal/server: accept JSON bodies with a missing or wrong Content-Type: fix a misleading \"no model id could be identified\" 404 when `curl -d` sent JSON as form-urlencoded; a middleware now relabels JSON object bodies as application/json and returns a 400 naming the expected format for unusable bodies (#1192) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v261","created_at":"2026-10-01T03:25:23Z","body":"\nThis release has a bunch of small compatibility improvements requested by the community.\nAlso the changelog summaries have been changed to only AI for the list below. These notes at\nthe top will be written by humans (or my dog) for humans. The AI's writing more correct but\nfuck it we have too much AI slop in our lives already.\n\n- [PR #1189](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1189) Increase ComfyUI concurrency limit from 50 to 999: fix ComfyUI stuck on the splash screen via /comfyui because one tab makes more parallel requests than the old minimum of 50 allowed (#1188) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1187](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1187) docker/unified: compile sm_70 in the CUDA 12 image for V100: fix ik-llama-server aborting on V100 GPUs, where only sm_61 PTX without a WMMA flash-attention kernel was available (#1185) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1158](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1158) Hardware Detection: detect Intel GPUs on Linux via xpu-smi, including dedicated Arc memory, and read the Metal version on macOS across system_profiler key names by [@anantshri](https://github.com/anantshri)\n- [PR #1183](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1183) docs/kb: document that tailcat.models accepts selectors: note that aliases, selectors, profile pins and peer model names are accepted, with a selector example by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n- [PR #1182](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1182) Build audio.cpp with static eSpeak-ng and install phoneme data: link eSpeak-ng statically and ship its phoneme data so Kokoro, SanoTTS and Inflect phonemization works without a writable cache (#1181) by [@mostlygeek](https://github.com/mostlygeek)\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v260","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:25:12Z","body":"\nThis release fixes a crash at startup on macOS 27 with Apple M6 hardware\n(#1178). Hardware detection reads the CPU frequency through gopsutil, which\nexpects a voltage-states5-sram property that is missing on M6. It passed the\nempty value straight to CFDataGetLength, which segfaulted before the server\ncould start listening.\n\nAs a temporary fix, gopsutil now points at a fork with the patch from\nshirou/gopsutil#2163, which checks for the missing property. This will be\nremoved once the upstream project picks up the patch. Some Go dependencies\nwere also updated as required by the newer gopsutil.\n\n- [PR #1180](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1180) go.mod: use gopsutil PR #2163 to fix darwin/arm64 crash: replace gopsutil with a patched fork that guards the CPU frequency probe against a missing property on Apple M6\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v259","created_at":"2026-09-26T06:21:41Z","body":"Maintainer note: \r\n\r\nThis release includes a bunch of small UI improvements and \r\nrequests from users. It also includes a contribution to detect DGX Spark\r\nhardware more accurately. \r\n\r\nI'm working on the AI sloppiness of the change log generation. The details \r\nare correct but I need to tune it. Perhaps I'll just keep writing notes at the \r\ntop like this :) \r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nLogging is split into three separate streams: proxy, upstream and HTTP access\r\nlogs. HTTP request lines used to be mixed in with the proxy log, which made it\r\nhard to search. They now have their own stream and their own tab in the log\r\nviewer. The logToStdout setting accepts a comma separated list of streams, such\r\nas \"proxy,http\", and the old values still work.\r\n\r\nUpgrading: log data has moved off GET /api/events to a new GET /api/events/logs\r\nendpoint. Pick streams with ?stream=proxy&stream=http. Tools that read logs\r\nfrom /api/events need to switch to the new endpoint.\r\n\r\nThe UI sidebar can be resized by dragging its edge, and the width is\r\nremembered. The model page has a new header that shows the model name, a\r\ncopyable ID, its state and how long it has been ready. The API also returns a\r\nnew readySince field for models that are ready.\r\n\r\nThe Hardware page now recognizes DGX Spark (GB10) systems. Before this, it\r\ncould not count sockets on arm64, labeled the unified memory as dedicated\r\nmemory it could not detect, showed only the efficiency cores and had no power\r\nfigure. It now shows the system model, the hybrid CPU layout, shared memory\r\nand the nominal 140 W SoC power.\r\n\r\nThe \"install as app\" prompt now works when apiKeys is set. The browser fetches\r\nthe web app manifest without an API key, so it got a 401. The manifest is now\r\nserved without auth, like the favicon.\r\n\r\nThe release process now checks for Claude or Codex before generating the\r\nchangelog and uses a newer model for it.\r\n\r\n- [PR #1177](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1177) internal/server: serve web app manifest without requiring auth: let browsers fetch site.webmanifest when apiKeys is set so the install prompt appears\r\n- AGENTS.md: revise contribution guidelines for PRs: agents check pull requests and issues against CONTRIBUTING.md and ask when there is a problem\r\n- [PR #1172](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1172) Refactor logging to support multiple streams and separate log endpoints: split proxy, upstream and HTTP logs, add /api/events/logs and allow a stream list in logToStdout\r\n- [PR #1163](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1163) hw: detect DGX Spark (GB10) systems: report the system model, hybrid CPU, sockets, shared memory and nominal power on GB10 boxes by [@lemassykoi](https://github.com/lemassykoi)\r\n- [PR #1173](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1173) ui: sidebar resize, model uptime tracking, small tweaks: drag to resize the sidebar and show how long each model has been ready\r\n- scripts/add-changelog.sh: use gpt-6-sol: update the model used to generate changelog entries with Codex\r\n- Makefile: detect harness before release: use Claude or Codex to generate the changelog and stop with an error when neither is installed\r\n\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v258","created_at":"2026-09-25T06:14:14Z","body":"\nTailcat is updated to v0.7.0 and now checks allowed clients in the HTTP\nhandler. A client that is not allowed gets a 403 instead of a TCP timeout,\nwhich makes peer connections much easier to troubleshoot, and changes to\ntailcat.allow now apply on hot reload. A bug that dropped the connection when\na node key was not recognized, which could leave clients hanging, now also\nreturns a 403. Peer connections recover better when the server disconnects,\nand they wait longer for the first response header by default.\n\nUpgrading: an empty tailcat.allow list now denies every client. To keep\nallowing anyone to connect, set tailcat.allow to \"*\".\n\nThe output of cmdStop goes to the process log again, the same as cmd. This was\nlost in an earlier change (#790). A cmdStop that leaves a background child\nholding its output open can no longer hang the stop, and hitting that wait\nlimit after a successful stop is logged as a warning instead of a failure.\n\nThe Models page shows a status icon for each target of the selected profile,\nand those models can be loaded and unloaded from the profile pane.\n\nThe unified Docker image adds mp3 support and native downloads to audio.cpp.\nThe image build also stops failing on untagged main-branch commits. Those\nbuilds fell back to looking up the \"latest\" release through the GitHub API,\nwhich rate limited the shared CI runners. The installers now build the commit\ndirectly and fall back to git tags when the API is not available.\n\nRelease notes on GitHub now use the CHANGELOG.md entry for the tag, and\nchangelog entries are written as plain-language summaries that credit outside\ncontributors.\n\n- release: improve generated changelog and release notes: generate readable changelog entries, credit outside contributors and use each entry as the GitHub release notes\n- [PR #1169](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1169) internal/tailcat: various reliability and bug fixes: return a 403 for unrecognized node keys, improve peer reconnects and raise the default time to first header\n- [PR #1170](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1170) ui: link profile targets and add load controls: show status and load/unload controls for profile target models by [@sousekd](https://github.com/sousekd)\n- [PR #1165](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1165) internal/process: log cmdStop stdout and stderr: send cmdStop output to the process log and stop a lingering child from hanging it by [@dividehex](https://github.com/dividehex)\n- [PR #1166](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1166) internal/tailcat: upgrade to tailcat v0.7.0 and use Server.Listen: check tailcat.allow per request, deny by default when empty and add a \"*\" wildcard\n- [PR #1157](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1157) docker/unified: audio.cpp add download and mp3 support: add mp3 and native download support\n- [PR #1156](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1156) docker/unified: fix vllm-wrapper build on untagged commits: build untagged commits directly and fall back to git tags when the GitHub API is rate limited\n\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v257","created_at":"2026-09-22T07:18:54Z","body":"## Changelog\n* f00d375a927f72d72e74ca86012be210f155c67b changelog: v257\n* 6f17d9e58eb04ab67d7af05fa9bfa6354c282f81 ui/playground: add a searchable model picker (#1153)\n* eeac3e6519cd65b371b75a0277cc893233015063 internal/capcompat: automatic context and modality discovery\n* 769dbacbcd2479d6de636c0675100f91844b3c9c internal/server,internal/config: Add tighter CORS controls\n* 29d10dfc102b54a13a67c9839882dc9691fbeece docs,server: improve comfyui endpoint and add a guide (#1145)\n* 96e6f94c018b51ae9cfc420b3166cfcace5bf97a internal/store: preserve request totals after pruning (#1136)\n* 6c36b88f4be6b560e811100d1eb364f418e03f92 internal/server: fix CORS handler returning too early\n* 2edad4a0a5b56fe6fbddb8537ee686ecc0a44181 internal/server: support proxy forwarded for headers\n* 76ab83bd8c491080a8d48b4f4e86cc4378cbc751 cmd/kubeswap/chart: fix the default demo's loopback bind (#1131)\n* 16c026ca935885f3205bf094e95f7d0d8a86453d .github/workflows: fix helm chat publishing (#1129)\n* c5753ce764595f8fe1ef77c45cb0ff80ae28d005 cmd/kubeswap: kubernetes backend for llama-swap (wrapper + helm chart) (#1114)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v256","created_at":"2026-09-17T07:08:37Z","body":"Maintainer note: This is the v256 Big-F-Release. I've been very busy and many small improvements have been squatting in main waiting to be unleashed. A few highlights: \r\n\r\n## Playground Chat UI improvements \r\n\r\n- tightened up the margins and cleaned up the design to be more mobile friendly\r\n- more timings and stats than you can shake a stick at\r\n- improved system prompt and added more hyper param controls (do who uses these anymore?) \r\n\r\n<img width=\"359\" height=\"625\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/06d526f3-688b-4a35-8479-17d047dd4055\" />\r\n<img width=\"358\" height=\"616\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e5a5c8e-3aa4-4aa9-bae7-9a97c339939b\" />\r\n\r\nThanks to contributors: \r\n\r\n - JoC - Started the model idle-time window after models become ready or restart [PR #1095](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1095).\r\n - Kris - Added live generation statistics to Chat [PR #1099](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/pull/1099).\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 6701d0d9d9dce7d698bcb6738ccacb75b0c27731 changelog: v256\r\n* 2409272b824156080a6af3b4997f147d5a337db5 CHANGELOG.md,docs: fix pull request link\r\n* b98a8ff76c89e88b338fc3754da3fc4b4e837126 changelog: add scripts and automation to generate changelog entries (#1125)\r\n* 40b36d9571eb1e865f78db34a59b4a676d4854a6 ui: make the playground chat responsive and lighter (#1120)\r\n* 0e1f7977bf5d607ce356873ac29d3751a93c78e5 internal/server: reduce zstd pool memory consumption (#1123)\r\n* aecf92e2e89b31eacdd1b778d83918a2445aa7db internal/store: split repository interfaces from the sqlite backend (#1122)\r\n* 21bc145a6fa6198c4d856fbb0830845c472b0ae4 process: start TTL idle window when model becomes ready (#1095)\r\n* 41ec321b6216d838488b2a7d936274ed227c0c5e internal/server: add global concurrency semaphore (#1110)\r\n* e1526c848060f702e402d75c6aa50a069f9dfd9c cmd/vllm-wrapper: use default timeouts\r\n* 8fa85899e424d47b81fa60aff08b238a793e2e2b internal/server: add tabbyapi usage data extraction (#1104)\r\n* 168632699383d440a5282b9da3612e741dd6cb7a ui: show chat stats in Help agent\r\n* acb77599647e2f508d681e23cefc898bae3258af ui: show live generation stats in Chat (#1099)\r\n* 6b181151549d80c49fedcaf408392d2309fa0edd ui: keep Work status bar stable while streaming (#1101)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v255","created_at":"2026-09-06T05:45:03Z","body":"## The Better Together Release\r\n\r\nThis release gets llama-swap + tailcat ready for use. If you haven't heard of [tailcat](https://github.com/tailscale/tailcat) it makes it easy to share models hosted by llama-swap with your friends or anyone over the Internet.  Tailcat is  \"Tailscale, without Tailscale by Tailscale\", which means you get Tailscale's security and connectivity magic without all the extra login and configuration overhead. \r\n\r\nHere's how it looks: \r\n\r\n<img width=\"979\" height=\"732\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5308791-aade-4c2c-853c-8d2a269f84c2\" />\r\n\r\nWith the token anyone can connect to your server securely and directly. No port forwarding, sharing IP addresses or setting firewall rules!\r\n\r\nMultiple llama-swap instances can be connected together as peer configurations also support tailcat! An easy to share peer configuration is automatically generated to share with friends:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"979\" height=\"562\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f99b944-9089-4bcd-ade9-30f188d54d69\" />\r\n\r\nTo get started generate your custom instructions with the built in Docs Agent: \r\n\r\n<img width=\"981\" height=\"748\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/880281e4-dd3b-448a-a198-997ae4b2d0d1\" />\r\n\r\nI would love [to hear your feedback](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/discussions/1097) and how you're using this cool new feature!\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 6c7f9587dd633d8d887321a0bf6c8de98bde18f3 docker/unified: add cuda13 with multi-platform support for arm64 (#1093)\r\n* 82ccfbf27f45d47ab6e21b5d2c8511e8489c8f01 filters: set-if-undefined params via \"?\" key suffix (#1075)\r\n* 41f143110debc3f55615f2191a1ed086efbccac3 ui/tailcat: mask connection token, add shareable peer config (#1091)\r\n* 8365956000a436dbeee275a9b90c24c053144f09 ui/help: raise Docs Agent max_tokens from 4096 to 65536 (#1089)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 7761aa13360ea379cb89366d07c2d08aa9f1ed10 tailcat: update to v0.6.0 (#1098)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v254","created_at":"2026-09-05T16:22:52Z","body":"## Thanks and Contributions \r\n\r\n- @jlacour-git contributed set-if-undefined for filters which makes setting default values easy!\r\n- various UI and tailcat improvements"},{"tag_name":"v253","created_at":"2026-09-04T06:32:30Z","body":"## Changelog\n* afba24b4e36628ed490c6bcb8020eb9e52d20e45 ui/help: refine Help agent topics and controls (#1088)\n* a77f107d7716a5f91dc1821fc62878165f174b98 Replace config path argument with jq query support (#1087)\n* 8a06d56b5444e62eccb6cbdf3616b232487b1125 tailcat: add private server and peer connectivity (#1074)\n* 7a14664d98f0e66bc68bba08548290ca0b469f98 docker/unified: make CUDA version and architectures configurable (#1072)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v252","created_at":"2026-08-30T18:57:20Z","body":"I've been very busy over the past few weeks and haven't had much time for llama-swap. First,  thank you for all the contributors in this release:\r\n\r\n- @sousekd for adding on_startup.profile. No more manual switching every time \r\n- @bernardogv for adding the -validate flag so configurations can be checked in one step\r\n- @chrispaulm for improving context limit compat in v1/models\r\n- @cphlipot for cmd/wol-proxy improvements\r\n- @ShinkoLab for improving IME (input method handler) support in the Playground\r\n- @WhyNotHugo for their keen eye catching a typo fix.\r\n\r\nThe key feature of is a Help agent in the Playground:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fb10ec1c-0061-4312-8331-ba5489cdeaa1\r\n\r\nI've finally accepted that writing documentation will never be prioritized over interesting engineering things. At the same time the complexity of the configuration can no longer be ignored. Having only config.example.yaml was fine in the beginning when there was only the `models` configuration but now there are dozens of knobs to configure concurrency, swapping, routing, remote peers, etc. \r\n\r\nSo now llama-swap has a built in Help agent. It's been tuned so a small agentic model can search and generate accurate answers to questions. It was fun to build: \r\n\r\n- an evaluation set so a frontier model can tune the performance of the a specialized agentic system. The baseline model, gemma-4-12B Q4_K_XL passes at 100%. It's a prototype and my first time using an eval set and an \"agent in a loop\" to optimize a whole system. \r\n- a core implementation of stateless MCP 2026-07-28 for doc search. Foundation for more llama-swap to be a stateless MCP proxy. No support for the stateful protocol stuff because I hate the design and think it should be deleted. \r\n- new UI elements for representing reasoning, tool calls, etc.\r\n- new docs/kb knowledge base that is easy to contribute to.\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* e31a1adee494bb7a578e2a97ec891b3e809899dc Split Docker build into per-project stages for CI (#1071)\r\n* e2d6f930f934eab6b65bd26701738db80ef2a7ee ui: improve Help page (#1070)\r\n* 6ffd67fdf2d935e1c564cd8c52078164e46327ab internal/reference: add indexed docs and /api/tools endpoints (#1054)\r\n* 32c3d66cd3bb96828750386a4306a3d87ae08154 config,server: add startup profile hook (#1053)\r\n* 1fc0490592174ffd6e4a79667b1f34474a470b11 expose context_window on models endpoint (#1063)\r\n* 51d1969c19af8d4983708137b8b495b269c5a27f cmd/wol-proxy: add -api-key option for use in health checks (#1055)\r\n* a6f5ae3d0d113071bb2b4111001fe18623ac7d3c cmd/wol-proxy: add liveness check (#1057)\r\n* 8a32e055f5bc6c7e07a138c8ffaca3a454bba78a Typo (#1049)\r\n* 4cd0247afab0be953c53942bf3eea3cfb006ecff config: accept video as an input and output modality (#1048)\r\n* bfbb99c6543b91d8e73493afa635c0487efa7455 cli: add -validate flag to check config and exit (#1046)\r\n* 9b4b3a08e743fe4682321096718026145833cc5e ui: ignore IME composition Enter in keydown handlers (#1045)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v251","created_at":"2026-08-23T06:58:47Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 4ec317589b21f58b64802c2b3371a179b9fdaa53 internal: record client disconnects as 499, not 200 or 502 (#1040)\n* 23432e65f0018b35bf47b778e923ba7b31552b1f internal/server: rate limit sendBuffer full warnings (#1043)\n* 0bdb3720199f530b622a1934c0db89f32c94819c internal/server: parse vLLM speculative decoding metrics (#1039)\n* cb536168c48976815a658e4e3db381774242e16f internal/swaputil: OpenAI-compatible error bodies (#1038)\n* 23c28febf1ccf3940aa01c077e46ff633da2a279 docker/unified: build audio.cpp as a deployment build (#1023)\n* b40d20e91660a0c6c0d3369aab410b42f591f1d2 ui: render ANSI colors in logs (#1019)\n* 08f1076cb777e787eba3f57170350aa09513341a ui-svelte: Add markdown activity export (#1020)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v250","created_at":"2026-08-14T15:45:40Z","body":"Lots contributors to thank on this release: \r\n\r\n- @einhander for greatly improving the `cmd/vllm-wrapper` and @depohmel for the initial contribution.\r\n- @chaserhkj for adding `/v1/task/run` endpoints for audio.cpp\r\n- @cphlipot for improving llama-server context compatibility and adding the `/models` endpoint \r\n- @noctrex for the cool new capabilities labels in the model UI (see screenshot below)\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1231\" height=\"1001\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cfe1ea82-e13b-46d7-af27-b1edad2b7d0b\" />\r\n\r\nThis release also updates the unifed docker container to come with: \r\n\r\n- audio.cpp \r\n- llama-bench\r\n- vllm-wrapper\r\n\r\nEnjoy!\r\n\r\nPS: check https://github.com/mostlygeek/retrocraft - Qwen 3.8 27B demo\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 60226b63776efac11e15828abe0bb302ec259699 docker/unified: add llama-bench, vllm-wrapper, audio.cpp (#1011)\r\n* 44a17d70df700aad8231d35ee5ead04c5c844738 README.md: reorder list of features\r\n* 3bccbefe4d79cdee88308405ee460e7bd3904f2b Support argv-based vLLM startup in `vllm-wrapper` (#979)\r\n* be683dc0ba0c0c44de0d55b8bbc464c882af8911 ui-svelte,internal/server: show capability tags on Models page (#1007)\r\n* 2edfa739c10ed8f56afcf14f2a1bfd40f6fb8b1f api: support /v1/task/run for audio.cpp (#982)\r\n* be5059823963512476fa6a9255e481fc5078aee5 AGENTS.md: tweak rules around pull requests\r\n* 3e583ade9b65879d69a5635a25213c9c432698a0 CONTRIBUTING.md: update rules\r\n* 038ae459422d74e2d22c83f0f1a00529bf395192 expose meta.n_ctx on models endpoint (#984)\r\n* 6333ee355d93d471e558957dfdf069f0c89d7fa3 router: add /models endpoint (#983)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v249","created_at":"2026-08-10T06:21:10Z","body":"If you use ComfyUI with llama-swap this release is  for you. A new /comfyui endpoint was added to make comfy and llama-swap more compatible. Now an idle comfyUI doesn’t block swapping or background HTTP requests cause comfy to load. \r\n\r\nTo use it create a model named comfyui_auto and llama-swap will take care of the rest. See issue #1001 for a comfyui and docker example to get started quickly. \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* f94c94ac61a142f15a4d156015bfb8c0511b3bbb various: improvements to code layout and naming (#1003)\r\n* 249797faad3475b5809fbd31802eb45441f19470 internal/server: add ComfyUI compatibility endpoint (#1002)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v248","created_at":"2026-08-08T17:26:02Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 00515cdf37beacfb440a04c12edd3423a19851ea internal/server,shared: preserve percent encoded in upstream (#988)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v247","created_at":"2026-08-04T05:35:06Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 40027d62fdc0cf08131973c02db2d4a7de172df1 ui-svelte: security update\n* 298848de59826d27fa824da6a2d958779419e7f6 internal/hw: detect inference host hardware (#978)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v246","created_at":"2026-08-03T02:52:39Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 22df230ba7890a4a3cfb7a2a98869529c2a674b3 ui-svelte: show configured selectors and strategies on Models page (#975)\n* 8d61908b13bfa4288827e5f117f937717b1b48c1 internal/perf: fix rocm-smi GPU memory utilization (#973)\n* 1f3c68edb6ef97f901008410232443ee6f8bcbfb docker: install rocm-smi for vulkan backend (#968)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v245","created_at":"2026-07-31T04:53:36Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 30470a4d7264df564aa355284fbbbeabecbd693c ui-svelte: show profiles on model page (#966)\n* 27782ab563bc40f1abeb88dee242be751ceafc02 AGENTS.md,CONTRIBUTING.md: update contribution guidelines (#964)\n* b9c3738d81aca5162537f249ed1d6d217c3ced04 docker: add -watch-config  (#963)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v244","created_at":"2026-07-28T05:49:23Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 0c4233363ec589c439b7f7d12eaae2346811098d internal/matrix: solve matrix expressions symbolically (#960)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v243","created_at":"2026-07-26T04:52:35Z","body":"## Spicy maintainer notes: \r\n\r\nv243 is a quality of life release. \r\n\r\n1. `cmd/vllm-wrapper` helps vLLM users avoid the long load times by communicating with an already running vLLM to load and sleep a model via its API. It hijacks the `model.cmd` and `model.cmdStop` parameters to send the commands. Neat. Thanks @depohmel for the contribution!\r\n2. Matrix sets can finally use full model IDs and using `var` is now optional. Using `var` was annoying for users who ultimately ran face first into a \"WTF is this naming limitation\" moment.  Even this frozen heart is melted by enough user tears. I'll work on lowering that threshold (maybe). \r\n3. #955 makes macros work where they are expected to (hopefully) in the configuration. The new approach does a multi-pass expansion over the yaml source. When there are no more macros to expand the configuration is unmarshalled into the typed configuration structure. Hopefully this is macro's final evolved form.  I consider this pokémon fully evolved. \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 4c50064e3d7ff44834cf1b12ab529befa79f22d6 internal/config: relax matrix model reference constraints (#957)\r\n* 4bffcfa539565f76c942b977faf5512ac14cc225 cmd/vllm-wrapper: add helper for sleep/wake (#941)\r\n* fa607fe04ec1dfe943e6bf036814b5c8a64e7d21 internal/config: refactor macro expansion (#955)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v242","created_at":"2026-07-25T07:03:25Z","body":"A bunch of changes today: \r\n\r\n- removed the 25MB filesize limit for audio files. This was pulled over by the agents (claude!!!!) from the backend file limit which was fixed a little while ago. Now,  upload big files and make your local machines cry! \r\n- fixed a bug found by @teru358 in #946 where TTL and model request could cause a deadlock. Opus 5 released just in time. It burned all the credits in my 5hr limit but the fix was pretty nice after a bit of back and forth. \r\n- introduce fully qualified peer model names. Remove the constraint that local and peer model Ids have to be unique. \r\n- with FQN for peer models the spillover selector can spill over to a remote model. Fun if you have multiple llama-swap rigs and want to tag team in the other one for more parallelism!  Qwen 3.6 27B Q8 at 25 tok/sec on the Framework Desktop is still faster than waiting at 0 tokens per second on the busy 3090s. \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 7aa7f52074d0aee99f9d1de8cea9cafb21289b67 internal/server,ui-svelte: add peer model namespaces (#950)\r\n* 5e9f887b5f287f2f9c7e389c8ada27a044fa2705 Fix process start race during concurrent stop operations (#949)\r\n* 12af351a63551c710029a631613ea966e10b1867 ui-svelte: remove audio file size limit (#948)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v241","created_at":"2026-07-22T03:54:55Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 8b61e3dcc9a662a773a42dfc551022fe28922de1 internal/server: implement selectors (#942)\n* c6adf57df1ac2e3dff2402dbb479cd5a133b6afe internal/server,shared: reduce request model body functions to one (#940)\n* 3e87c022c478a46bb9c72a8cb8f9808a3922e4e5 internal/server: add support for profiles  (#935)\n* 378a26e16654f547595c512533b21042e43d710c ui-svelte: add support for different v1/audio/voices response formats (#932)\n* fc8b29f0546b376f5be5fe27971c81608fe0974a docker: add FFmpeg support for whisper.cpp (#785)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v240","created_at":"2026-07-15T01:01:54Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 6b5320de5dc7f6f9f3266afd37a707279be271ca internal/server: expand inflight request details (#923)\n* cd22a8c0109242dff4d73388e03a4e4bff6f2f73 Add configurable UnloadTimeout variable (#904)\n* 61f83ac1a49b654e25a15f149d68b615f43a318b ui-svelte: code-split routes and trim highlight.js/chart.js bundles (#925)\n* 74629732ea9e66fc6ca692e29f486af0d06007aa .coderabbit.yaml: disable annoying unit test creation\n* 799eedb32d003960a59041099280ac91a0795fec internal/config: preserve yaml anchors in capabilities (#918)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v239","created_at":"2026-07-11T21:26:27Z","body":"## Changelog\n* dd81801d7bfa1a9100ac7af0e579731650b357e6 internal/config: preserve yaml anchors in capabilities\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v238","created_at":"2026-07-11T05:15:48Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 3c7946166d5315b93d786cb002b91f2b0e3d6385 internal/server: improve vllm response metric calculation (#913)\n* 8945d2b766cf0062b20ad8571386705d2355b368 internal/config: resolve macros in capabilities fields (#907)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v237","created_at":"2026-07-10T06:10:28Z","body":"## Notes\r\n\r\n- Support for the new metrics and usage data in vllm responses\r\n- Fix some small UI nits \r\n- Remove the 10sec wait delay in wol-proxy. \r\n  - random: mine's been running for months, all those 10s waits of my life I wasted everytime I updated my config! \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 9e63971d3ecaa63e5c6d57f08596c43aeb18e181 ui-svelte: activity logs older than a day show a timestamp (#911)\r\n* 0e5807aaa53ff1a2ed06d52204accc5011b83fef internal/server: support vLLM metrics (#910)\r\n* ca723d3b9e09b82e06bb6d9f8b2fc1f71f82038b cmd/wol-proxy: remove lag when llama-swap restarts (#909)\r\n* fdda55e466444d804615a261d5bb53b1c9c91e80 Remove Star History section from README\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v236","created_at":"2026-07-07T06:36:00Z","body":"## Changelog\n* b834706bcdb4d6cb3847983fd0eadd0f0d23ed56 internal/server: add status to v1/models for llama-server (#901)\n* 6291bb88697c50cbe6b1508eeacba8db568263d9 internal/store: persist activity metrics to sqlite (#898)\n* 579b1e7bed3dd1659fd4e45ee9b1fc50240767f2 fix starhistory\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v235","created_at":"2026-07-03T16:19:44Z","body":"## Changelog\n* c59816bace800e1630ca8791541b4a53a9705f9b internal/server: show inflight activity requests (#895)\n* d8ed077f7a3018da649292330a5a917e6d1fe2ec Add llama-tts binary (#894)\n* 0d2d8511706d30ce62f69c7b7ca0ee9bff589042 Makefile: improve build version stamping (#891)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v234","created_at":"2026-06-30T22:19:38Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 4a6b8a89915426754d22441d6fb6c6912d3af0ea internal/router: reject concurrency excess before streaming (#889)\n* 3023ab4da07462cc96c2daf01b6501266b3bab27 add /props to modelGetRoutes (#886)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v233","created_at":"2026-06-29T19:12:33Z","body":"Bug and Performance improvements for the UI\r\n\r\n- fixed streaming logs blocking llama-server inference. Logs are pushed to connected UI clients via an async channel now so if they are slow it does not affect reading from stdout of llama-server\r\n- replaced the placeholder.txt with a go build tag approach - fix CI\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 083e42105cb797b0bd9df174ab4dc8aa4a7e9c1a internal/logmon: decouple log broadcast from Write (#878)\r\n* a667c57d2ead6be4adaa0088c7cd413bb9984a77 internal/server: gate UI embed behind embed_ui build tag (#880)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v232","created_at":"2026-06-29T05:30:35Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 25b27cb9a05679a8f3c751f3586c9f5c27ad8875 ui-svelte: add rounded borders\n* 18cc8546c664fdca7975146ceb19b16dd2f5d527 update hero image\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v231","created_at":"2026-06-28T22:39:09Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 74e92b05c5754e5473caf73dab6952de43db6bd1 Update screenshots\n* da862efa1b45438784f6f5502bda4085f79f095f ui: add shadcn-svelte foundation and theming (#877)\n* 0a25b3bd31786abd6f0bfb533b87ea08a23198e5 AGENTS.md: small tweaks\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v230","created_at":"2026-06-25T03:48:51Z","body":"This release adds the -config-dir flag! Using a config-dir it’s now possible to split huge config.yaml files into fragments that get automatically merged together. \r\n\r\nYou can have one model per file and combined with -watch-config models can be enabled or disable by moving them in or out of -config-dir. \r\n\r\nThe -config and -config-dir flags are compatible and can be used at the same time or exclusively. \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 32bc7813261000228ea5274d89a8c89e7cce2725 internal/config,watcher: add -config-dir (#873)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v229","created_at":"2026-06-21T20:49:53Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 316ad63f765365c7ea100a7270de12eeffc1190f config,server: add upstream.ignorePaths (#869)\n* e37077a96383a4877827ea468c12eb08a3f5ca7c feat: hide performance menu item if disabled (#832)\n* eff9b604340a68475cec013ecb317690eaf8d58c server: capture failed (non-200) LLM requests (#862)\n* 9bcddad91b36adf8e5bfb7d7fa28b58d8995bca2 internal/server,ui: add new Acitivty page column - Drafted (#859)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v228","created_at":"2026-06-18T00:38:52Z","body":"## Changelog\n* a15e47922c3db3e24df75b2648acad5acafeda4b proxy: meter /upstream requests via metrics middleware (#858)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v227","created_at":"2026-06-17T04:49:09Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 0ab214d1c8b04bc7bd76ec777bf0f41a7b1ac604 perf: add vendor-agnostic GPU monitoring for Windows (experimental) (#779)\n* d07b063ab6e02ad2edb7d925da0a5b4b4822ee6c internal/server,shared: support request metadata (#850)\n* 826210dac9bbbaa5d2b925f2bfcd5f0f60b5859a .coderabbit.yaml: disable unit_tests\n* 6cf1317341a620fc1225b83c4e5402640aabc725 schedule,shared: move concurrency 429 limits into scheduler code (#849)\n* 8e84b2ec4f7c44b9fda8c91e38d9e50015583e1b README.md: add macports install option to README (#848)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v226","created_at":"2026-06-14T20:38:10Z","body":"## Changelog\n* ed77385d08225adbe447c89eb9a1b098a72ebcfb ui: improve manual model load and cancel (#847)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v225","created_at":"2026-06-14T06:23:19Z","body":"## Model Capabilities \r\n\r\nThe new `capabilities` configuration option makes it easy to define what modalities the model supports for input and output. Here is what the configuration looks like: \r\n\r\n```yaml\r\nmodels:\r\n    example_model:    \r\n      # capabilities: defines what the model accepts for input, output and other metadata\r\n      # - optional; omitted or all-zero means no capabilities\r\n      # - used in v1/models to inform clients what the model can do\r\n      capabilities:\r\n        # in: list of modalities understood by the model\r\n        # - default: []\r\n        # - valid: text, audio, image\r\n        in:\r\n          - text\r\n          - audio\r\n          - image\r\n        # out: list of modalities generated by the model\r\n        # - default: []\r\n        # - valid: text, audio, image\r\n        out:\r\n          - text\r\n          - audio\r\n          - image\r\n        # tools: the model supports function calling\r\n        # - default: false\r\n        tools: true\r\n  \r\n        # reranker: the model supports the /v1/rerank endpoint\r\n        # - default: false\r\n        reranker: false\r\n  \r\n        # context: the maximum token context length supported\r\n        # - default: 0\r\n        # - must be an integer > 0\r\n        context: 32000\r\n\r\n    # capabilities can be written in a very condensed form\r\n    image_gen:\r\n        capabilities:\r\n            in: [text]\r\n            out: [image]\r\n    speech_to_text:\r\n        capabilities:\r\n            in: [text]\r\n            out: [audio]\r\n    transcription:\r\n        capabilities:\r\n            in: [audio]\r\n            out: [text]\r\n    reranker:\r\n        capabilities:\r\n          reranker: true\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen a client calls `v1/models` it will generate metadata that is compatible with mistral, openrouter and huggingface chat-ui formats. \r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"data\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"image_gen\",\r\n      \"object\": \"model\",\r\n      \"created\": 1781420051,\r\n      \"owned_by\": \"llama-swap\",\r\n      \"architecture\": {\r\n        \"input_modalities\": [\r\n          \"text\"\r\n        ],\r\n        \"modality\": \"text->image\",\r\n        \"output_modalities\": [\r\n          \"image\"\r\n        ]\r\n      },\r\n      \"capabilities\": {\r\n        \"image_generation\": true\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"reranker\",\r\n      \"object\": \"model\",\r\n      \"created\": 1781420051,\r\n      \"owned_by\": \"llama-swap\",\r\n      \"capabilities\": {\r\n        \"reranker\": true\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"speech_to_text\",\r\n      \"object\": \"model\",\r\n      \"created\": 1781420051,\r\n      \"owned_by\": \"llama-swap\",\r\n      \"architecture\": {\r\n        \"input_modalities\": [\r\n          \"text\"\r\n        ],\r\n        \"modality\": \"text->audio\",\r\n        \"output_modalities\": [\r\n          \"audio\"\r\n        ]\r\n      },\r\n      \"capabilities\": {\r\n        \"audio_speech\": true\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"id\": \"transcription\",\r\n      \"object\": \"model\",\r\n      \"created\": 1781420051,\r\n      \"owned_by\": \"llama-swap\",\r\n      \"architecture\": {\r\n        \"input_modalities\": [\r\n          \"audio\"\r\n        ],\r\n        \"modality\": \"audio->text\",\r\n        \"output_modalities\": [\r\n          \"text\"\r\n        ]\r\n      },\r\n      \"capabilities\": {\r\n        \"audio_transcriptions\": true\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"object\": \"list\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Other changes\r\n\r\n- Implementation of a new scheduler backend (#823). No functional changes for users but will make implementing different scheduling and swapping strategies a bit easier. This is just the first step and the goal is for anyone to customize llama-swap's behaviour with by implementing the new interfaces. \r\n- #839 is a follow up to improve abstractions and implementation boundaries for new schedulers / swappers\r\n  - it also resolved the long standing #717! If you have api keys set in the configuration the UI will prompt for a password now :) \r\n  - the /metrics endpoint requires an api key now. HTTP Basic Auth is supported so prometheus integration is a single step.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 92b90447e894a5579132b15f1657a8175a3826f6 Model capabilities 734 (#842)\r\n* 62aea0e83df49f5d2722031df4818e79d15f1fef internal/router,server,shared: refactor auth, libs (#839)\r\n* 8c660dcb9077950525e5d46bf42ec4b756517cab main: gofmt\r\n* f6877b81755ca4a3cf25aaf4ac9f70d1a289f95e main: show message when listening on network (#836)\r\n* 9b3a33d7b9c3bd742d7c3dd4755e84f637ffdc77 Implement new scheduler  (#823)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v224","created_at":"2026-06-10T04:37:53Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 0cfe5a6639a91b55ec1d8f5d122fb9cf78debd91 Makefile,internal: fix websocket regression and other small things (#830)\n* 44e1501e8118588279e3874f3b8ee848548af808 internal/process,server: fix unload regression (#828)\n* 46cea36bc2d7a23b8104f4b1ee867f901b7c9c08 proxy: remove legacy code. Thanks champ 🫡 (#822)\n* ccfba0df28ab4d5dcace9056469cbc929249696b docker: fix arm64 cpu image downloading amd64 llama-swap binary (#819)\n* ddfae90b19762f1f32ea00cc67e9b67510f9e6db Change cron schedule for container builds\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v223","created_at":"2026-06-04T04:51:03Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 29d3d9ba206f58e91c931d30387f455efc64d245 perf: add macOS GPU monitoring via mactop and ioreg (#816)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v222","created_at":"2026-06-01T07:45:30Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 9be9a87fa019e542622f2a9c3f18bb715ebeb175 internal/process: improve windows shutdown behaviour (#808)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v221","created_at":"2026-05-31T17:11:12Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 6ea551362e3791f0922bd13356bf7a5c45766fc7 process,router: make model shutdown and load-streaming robust\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v220","created_at":"2026-05-31T00:04:30Z","body":"Another release? Who needs to touch grass? \r\n\r\nThis release includes a small patch by first time contributor @Luiszzzor. As well a new load and concurrency testing tool has been added to the Playground. It's easier to show than tell so check out this demo video with a swap matrix example: \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/88e24794-aa26-4db4-82b9-0c618b3ce0f3\r\n\r\nSide note: I forgot to mention in the video that to support more than 5 or 6 (depending on your browser) concurrent requests you will need a valid TLS certificate. llama-swap supports http/2 however that requires https. In the demo I run it on my tailnet with `tailscale serve 8080` which generates the Let's Encrypt cert for me. \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 03d58e53fa35ec26b03ce5117cf55bad6ead662c Add load testing tool to the UI (#805)\r\n* c790d0ee03e514b2c83a54dfc2894187e155ce83 fix: update the concurrency middleware to respond with a JSON payload (#798)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v219","created_at":"2026-05-29T22:27:08Z","body":"## Notes\r\n\r\nIncluding details for v218 (broken) and PR #790. \r\n\r\nllama-swap has a new routing backend. What started as a small experiment to improve the concurrency handling exploded into a full refactor of the backend. For users this the biggest change is swapping is more efficient. Requests are collated so requests for models that are already loaded will take precedence over those that awaiting loading. \r\n\r\nIt looks like: \r\n\r\n```\r\nnew router: A B A B A B -> A A A B B B\r\nold router: A B A B A B -> A B A B A B \r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, just doing that wouldn't require a 12,009 line PR. There were a lot of architectural changes that makes developer quality of life a bit easier. Redundant code was removed, repo organization is centralized around the internal/ packages, new funny loading remarks were added, etc. \r\n\r\nAlso a new concurrency tester sneaked in under cmd/concurrency-tester. \r\n\r\n<img width=\"2816\" height=\"1590\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7118447b-0a35-4981-a624-4b2442865e66\" />\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 4ca9c478a2fb1030ce789bbdb4f063825a958a2e Makefile,internal/server: various release tweaks\r\n* 146a9eab24f0d60acbc81abc13d6979131ede47b ui-svelte: update build directory (#801)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v218","created_at":"2026-05-29T04:47:01Z","body":"This one has a bug where the release did not include the UI. Use v219 instead. \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 02e015fa49d6d3871d6f57e15373e7fb7051062c Introduce new routing backend (#790)\r\n* 63bc2663951241cf1fd19e8253b498a79e11a76a Add new power draw column header for rocm-smi monitoring (#788)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v217","created_at":"2026-05-21T00:59:49Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 636b53e70ff7c834e92a97ef2bb556ee60ca2f85 Improve rocm-smi performance monitoring (#775)\n* 59cd3b690d2dda976850e1f6efc41f8efb13cbc5 Added Windows performance monitoring using nvidia-smi (#773)\n* 5d1e62d2245d336e5ec569c650bba7d28b0f424d Disable auto review feature in coderabbit config\n* dbb869d0199014a3172f6c1ed806734d8e6ce47f Increase inactivity thresholds for stale issues\n* 26bb17e57e8eb7fd8a4cea2294439ac8cb89fc80 config.example.yaml: Improve matrix vs groups info\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v216","created_at":"2026-05-17T18:45:56Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 2982dd3d40c79272335da961b519ba6170c750f6 ui-svelte: update link to performance discussion thread\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v215","created_at":"2026-05-17T14:58:26Z","body":"Adds ROCm support to the new experimental performance monitor. \r\nThank you to @knguyen298 for this patch. \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 79dc87f88155ff1b94dada40f0461520c2798017 Add ROCm stats via rocm-smi (#767)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v214","created_at":"2026-05-15T21:42:44Z","body":"This release fixes a couple of small bugs in the UI and the new performance monitor\r\n\r\n## Contributors\r\n\r\n- @krzychdre (#760) for finding and fixing the negative counting in the UI\r\n- @cdwaage (#759) for fixing the bug in the nvidia-smi fallback for the performance monitor\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* b2fcc2daa146b67903bebad2e0226639cdc13411 ui-svelte: fix cached tokens total counting -1 sentinel (#760)\r\n* 6a9c4efc8f0d428e809f1b102776eb9b912a495e fix: use --loop instead of -loop for nvidia-smi (driver 540+ compat) (#759)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v213","created_at":"2026-05-15T04:56:04Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 0c813e44d10524262d7f386761c1aa697421c47b ui-svelte: package updates\n* fe71e8a6ea4cbf8618777d07a6e4fd423799d8c1 proxy,ui-svelte: improve support for v1/messages and v1/responses (#758)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v212","created_at":"2026-05-14T05:12:02Z","body":"This release packs a lot into it. It introduces a new experimental performance monitor for linux machines first. In the UI there is a new tab that will show up to the last hour of statistics: \r\n\r\n<img width=\"1840\" height=\"2420\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/65fbecc6-f75e-45da-8a3f-8a59cc093d1a\" />\r\n\r\nAdditionally a `/metrics` for the common prometheus and grafana combo. A [grafana dashboard](https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap/blob/main/docs/grafana/example-dashboard.json) example is provided to get you started. It looks like this: \r\n\r\n<img width=\"2238\" height=\"1592\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51d48217-ab28-47d0-9d09-18804bdf1fdb\" />\r\n\r\n## Other small changes\r\n\r\n- versionless API endpoints were added that do not require the v1/ prefix. These help with upstream peers like z.ai that do not follow the v1 versioning convention\r\n- the `-watch-config` system has been refactored. It supports a mounting the config file into a docker container now. This removes the requirement to mount a directory with the config in it. \r\n\r\n## Contributions from the community\r\n\r\nMuch thanks to @bankjaneo (#741), @rhtenhove (#746), @sousekd (#753). \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* aac7b8745ab5fc793c3d146ca74be4faa0a59804 ci: set go-version-file in release workflow\r\n* 4e606feff02eece1756041487a9bf19193a53dcf ci: fix workflow bugs in release and go-ci\r\n* a4b91e08cf6f161b7d18328838004db24e1fc10b Changes and fixes before the release (docs/small tweaks) (#750)\r\n* 3e3646f9f9504e83d026779ad3cccae82dee3e8c perf: ignore LACT devices reporting zero VRAM (#753)\r\n* a01afe261bc4265635f9d40ac4e543b9266ac7ca ci: use manifest-aware cleanup action for multi-arch :cpu (#751)\r\n* 174e8562aa29d2908c09ecc764806ca5e6c43724 Multi arch cpu (#746)\r\n* 085b54bc888a4b4168e31fe75c4c585bfd3013d0 proxy: fix data race in /running endpoint and typo in error message (#748)\r\n* 2be3416baa83db5f202b8a187b1d99e3e378b23c ui: add auto theme switch mode based on system theme (#741)\r\n* 7e3e94a08a6b623e4fc3ad5f2c695f78bd0d943c proxy,ui: add performance monitoring with Prometheus metrics (#743)\r\n* e261745c66969c119eed1de740380187b365d458 proxy: add versionless API endpoint (#733)\r\n* 11b7913287e15a5c6cf82ec33af5824f516c92e1 llama-swap.go: remove debounce, replace fmt.Printlns (#731)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v211","created_at":"2026-05-01T23:43:20Z","body":"## Changelog\n* c79114d40a9a82e65d19a629e069c9b37efb8c33 proxy: fix logger not checking matrix for processes\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v210","created_at":"2026-05-01T02:51:28Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 430166d5eb182af84660b21a9820056d3b0e45b8 proxy: fix zero duration for non streaming responses (#723)\n* 5b4beaceef199bd42627588543d8512dafc784e1 fix: ?no-history flag and improve /logs monitoring docs (#721)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v209","created_at":"2026-04-29T03:33:03Z","body":"## Changelog\n* fd3c28ffc50b15e1031517b88040d656c34b6a79 Refactor Activity Page (#710)\n* a846c4f18cb583fe8e04d142ea8dc677e6637acc config: remove hard cap on macro length (#718)\n* 5bae33a7699e7849c117f6c66b5bc91a0d96f945 ui-svelte: default theme to user preferred color scheme (#712)\n* 8f4ff01f935557fb467c7d0eca25e8ea0bca2fb8 ui-svelte: make it easier to toggle panels in logs view\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v208","created_at":"2026-04-26T20:11:48Z","body":"## Changelog\n* e8d4384cd2099d02394ad48e465cae2b9b4c95f1 ui-svelte: support reasoning and reasoning_content (#708)\n* ce28485be256461c5819433dc0ab8137956dafcd ui-svelte: add prompt processing histogram (#705)\n* 3cd7837b1f5dc9dc555e3fe859ca57b0227d52e4 fix: support architecture-specific download URLs in install script (#698)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v207","created_at":"2026-04-23T06:42:39Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 0b31ccacc123bcc92a0fbdf5ebd8dab35e3f3ce2 ui-svelte: fix histogram calculation (#695)\n* 5938dbee8f164c9aa0a93e6147d54bc233c0ae27 Push unified docker images on scheduled runs (#694)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v206","created_at":"2026-04-23T06:42:39Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 0b31ccacc123bcc92a0fbdf5ebd8dab35e3f3ce2 ui-svelte: fix histogram calculation (#695)\n* 5938dbee8f164c9aa0a93e6147d54bc233c0ae27 Push unified docker images on scheduled runs (#694)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v205","created_at":"2026-04-22T06:21:48Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 66639e83f7be4f1354817e45321f50bdb8e3227d proxy: replace fsnotify with stat-poll watcher and add SIGHUP reload (#685)\n* 625b29672050f81ea9c4d3fae3b68bf2c2d6fd30 docker/unified: add uv via pip install (#681)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v204","created_at":"2026-04-20T07:21:11Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 231e62291c9a0c989c7a565adf684878736484a4 proxy: fix matrix race and process stop bug (#677)\n* 57ac666598308dea57c3eb56b2a564164dd68abf .github/workflows: tweak push ghcr conditional (#676)\n* 69728301f55325abdbfd96248319374026862f5a .github/workflows: add toggle for pushing unified images to github (#672)\n* c176fa70f11e5b84f884e9e1b0bb15e3f58cade9 docker/unified: add spirv-headers to fix vulkan build (#669)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v203","created_at":"2026-04-18T06:29:37Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 5e3c646829c5d6cba167e1db0a0acbdd61ae895e proxy: compress captures with zstd (#668)\n* c3f0d43e6ee17e7b646f76b1c442481ea1ea2bc8 proxy: fix race conditions during swap (#667)\n* f6cf9f5844ab66bcbde3bdd76b4da32543336602 proxy: Refactor tests  (#660)\n* 121fd93ad889619c77d9aeecedc8befc03e89aa8 Makefile: restore linux arm64 targets\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v202","created_at":"2026-04-15T05:01:03Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 17233e927895b059a793c47f1e7317b481ab5f5d docs: update configuration.md for matrix\n* 4866d16c3e7681e102bfde47bc5ec49fa7889da6 README.md: update to use matrix instead of groups\n* 35193f82f11b516f68c90bb31816cf50de2f9ad1 proxy: add swap matrix with solver-based model swapping (#646)\n* 40e39f7a86a2591a5afe8f8215377cd9f41e8573 ui-svelte: fix security issues (#649)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v201","created_at":"2026-04-12T03:42:13Z","body":"## Changelog\n* a9d840ffd720ddbda02d857879f4f76107fbb086 proxy,proxy/config: restore timeouts to pre PR 619 (#648)\n* 7b2b82777fcf2b159d8b1a75650def9c18202909 docker/unified: derive rootless image from root container (#644)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v200","created_at":"2026-04-07T10:05:53Z","body":"## Changelog\n* d87f0ce2c534f1586e1884b9b6b547dea4608993 docker/unified: publish rootless image variant (#630)\n* 06bc6a614c3c7e938915fb7d12f59c5f9bdaacdd proxy: preserve wall-clock duration in metrics (#629)\n* a37b4866d8a5e4d8e1e1fe63a63db2d144ba3019 proxy: add configurable HTTP timeouts for models and peers (#619)\n* 981910d734ae21430dc2e28ec364550364a596f5 ci: validate config.example.yaml against config-schema.json (#627)\n* a185efe37ea685daeb2dc652ab9e7bef0f159bef docker: make CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES configurable via build arg (#625)\n* 1dd1aadf93ee2489d0ce6857214c91382eede355 docker/unified: add ik_llama.cpp to CUDA container (#620)\n* 955900972a459252febfe17008308385b7ae3196 add /sdapi to list of supported endpoints\n* c2c8cfaf8136e588b92bd1e15670ae606354d506 docker/unified: build llama.cpp with static libraries (#616)\n* 1e440770eac543c395d9ceaf89e3f77250163ae7 ci: fix matrix exclude for scheduled docker workflow (#610)\n* c794273c83b7602ff2f209cc4f533ee5cf663c04 docker/unified,.github: fix unified build (#606)\n* 6574a52cbbb1f227e8ca2375c805875f1bd965ba build(deps): bump picomatch from 4.0.3 to 4.0.4 in /ui-svelte (#605)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v199","created_at":"2026-03-25T14:26:13Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 8fabc75634564a3f803b890c82ab8711ad1ea063 docker/unified: vulkan build fixes (#600)\n* e5e7391b6d2fd3cda3d6f484ad3400ccf23c0b4c .github,docker/unified: include vulkan build (#599)\n* 2c282dccad1c56c16c794fdfddcf64ac29f23fa6 .github,docker/unified: improve caching and fix bugs (#598)\n* 916d13f5bd4c47eeaf32f9598a9745bfa2e15cce .github/workflows,docker/unified: add cuda based unified container (#597)\n* a3725e7d091cb66b7beb8a284451dd593b53bbcb Update go.mod to 1.26.1 (#593)\n* 15bd55d3a9dc98a5e52180979171bcdc553e28e9 proxy, ui-svelte: add /sdapi/v1 endpoint support (#587)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v198","created_at":"2026-03-13T23:50:12Z","body":"## Changelog\n* c3c258a55d5d0f0fc4e74b27747fae49dbf1e2be proxy: fix metrics capture for v1/responses (#586)\n* 29a38fde0d041cc1863c0d94623909f0f02ea859 ui-svelte: upgrade to vite 8 (#585)\n* d569681daaa71e27def618f1bdb2ef813f78389d Change model sorting to natural order (#582)\n* 24efdb76b1b46d7dd5c85cb7a030d94f26a01d38 config: add macro support for name and description fields (#578)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v197","created_at":"2026-03-02T05:02:12Z","body":"## Changelog\n* cc77139ff86da7055798c8b5dead414752e0b2f4 proxy,proxy/config: add global TTL feature (#554)\n* 390a35bf9321c2ed85c3233957bc07451e18d201 ui-svelte: add copy button to markdown code blocks (#537)\n* 181f71ca11583e251ca4607e5e099ea47e8a7327 .github,docker: add cuda13 architecture support (#551)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v196","created_at":"2026-02-28T07:47:52Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 49546e2cf2d7089bafc463a51677b4843f4627ec ui: fix text size svg\n* 2c078964f4abd9c9ecdfe2e738619a95fb41e7dc Update README with additional images\n* 175bb36fb19e5447cad3a06cf366aba96ada77e6 Revise README description for clarity and detail\n* aedb64047155b37483e82e7f133fc09f30ba8715 Enhance web UI section in README\n* 2f377f6dc69937c3da92d838c3d913768b4aa175 ui: add OGG audio format support to transcription playground (#544)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v195","created_at":"2026-02-22T05:59:14Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 64e4c79fc310f9d36606016ffbaa164386364fc5 ui: add Rerank tab to playground (#536)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v194","created_at":"2026-02-20T06:21:10Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 19fb5f35e937fc0083c6c56bf74e19fc44334fff proxy: implement setParamsByID filter (#535)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v193","created_at":"2026-02-19T03:47:37Z","body":"## Changelog\n* b45102bde80d747a9f065e75c14a4229ea2b007a ui: smart auto-scroll in LogPanel (#530)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v192","created_at":"2026-02-16T17:41:15Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 1688bdd1e984cfa532a22106c7ce69ecea3f51d5 proxy, ui: add pending requests count to the main dashboard (#516)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v191","created_at":"2026-02-16T05:31:30Z","body":"## Changelog\n* d33d51fa75a8cada78d0369467f8e6a2c89a171a .coderabbit.yaml,AGENTS.md: small tweaks\n* e3bf0655749906078a87828208e62f739bce7a70 ui: persist playground state across route navigation (#525)\n* 3e521440588ef8a881ae82c584292f72c86171c0 ui-svelte: incremental rendering of chat messages in the Playground (#520)\n* d5e52d7d001dab73bd3137b641aa4ac89bba3f2b build: disable provenance attestations in container builds (#523)\n* 17e5263a76f6b93c8a431879de6a54f87394cfa4 .github/workflows: fix expired token in publishing images (#522)\n* 8d6d949ec352a2f2c52f2f8efef198f1ad1e3e60 proxy: support timings for /infill from llama-server (#510)\n* b5fde8eb6d86f0e61cea2c3fde8abe628b9a93bc proxy,ui-svelte: add request/response capturing (#508)\n* 7eef5defb868656ac93db343c3d677792bb1a71d docs: add stable-diffusion.cpp references (#506)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v190","created_at":"2026-02-08T00:54:02Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 4b4ee7015463886c92c2b1b0cf07ace45fb4d923 proxy: support timings for /infill from llama-server\n* b5fde8eb6d86f0e61cea2c3fde8abe628b9a93bc proxy,ui-svelte: add request/response capturing (#508)\n* 7eef5defb868656ac93db343c3d677792bb1a71d docs: add stable-diffusion.cpp references (#506)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v189","created_at":"2026-02-02T00:17:26Z","body":"## Changelog\n* bc01e6f539c4148161db4fe1d2c12597fda1a27a build: add stable-diffusion server to musa and vulkan container images (#504)\n* 0462e3dc3ff42da270e7795f8e867743560fcba6 Reorganize UI controls and improve form interactions (#500)\n* 7b20fc011b558a9fd792f95d1a530431d7290503 Add path filters to CI workflows and create UI test workflow (#501)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v188","created_at":"2026-02-01T06:49:13Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 20738f36239e26d487c938fe29e6398f9f42f0d0 proxy,ui-svelte: replace old UI with svelte+playground\n* cdea7d16bd3d88d58ea95c8537f0a4ff1d1bff35 proxy/config: skip env macros in YAML comment lines (#496)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v187","created_at":"2026-01-29T05:40:18Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 5de387dbf970e8be0777c1b6956a65150107a158 ui: fix node-tar vulnerability\n* 6f8e7ccb579c96ecc65663a17c0265ceb43495f4 .github/workflows: switch release.yml to build ui-svelte\n* 4384315b44cee2fe50cb3cee99051c8c0c817d9f ui-svelte: add Svelte port of React UI (#487)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v186","created_at":"2026-01-22T16:43:36Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 6439ab1515d6de577611fdc323d91d217d916493 ui: add peer:true in package-lock.json\n* f94226122ca0a1ea9ed839b90a6a973f48d9512d build(deps-dev): bump tar from 7.5.3 to 7.5.6 in /ui (#477)\n* 7493618fdca22cec2d28bc1b33e63cf37785ad6b Add count_tokens api proxying (#476)\n* 205efd40a14de0c216462d29bab6ee90580fba62 proxy: extend /running endpoint with additional process data (#474)\n* 14207f8492408377479d29cf609b76a51a3a38f4 ui: npm security update\n* 4e850c2834a38e029321d75a58e4c8b4bcf6f124 config: refactor macro substitution in configuration (#470)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v185","created_at":"2026-01-17T07:10:50Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 75fced579e3ee4239dc9e93c259201dbcf966590 config: support macros in peer apiKey and filters (#469)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v184","created_at":"2026-01-17T06:43:25Z","body":"## Changelog\n* b73f367f22b6a7289dfeef1989ead8881bbfe181 config-schema.json,config.example.yaml: Update examples and schema\n* 8f2137c72b04a53a6a3aedc50178cd4dc8dde968 config: support environment variable macros in apiKeys (#467)\n* 124007cc985db0df0ad5ca7e93b449432896d88d config: add environment variable macros (#466)\n* eb5bfff0b00b4595b2e43b641c2767ed9887c392 proxy: unify filtering for local models and peers\n* 3edb180c088ae55f480be2090f3ecbf89ffaafa8 ci: free up disk space before ROCm container build (#460)\n* 66d555e625bcbfd8b1ab28a0eb5c21b5f78ca9a5 Improve container build reliability (#457)\n* 4f863fd9fc8ce5261f17df5d227efe1c3efc5d58 CLAUDE.md: tweak instructions\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v183","created_at":"2026-01-09T00:13:09Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 267c0304570eeaea800b93f543c88439396de5be ui: update react-router-dom to 7.12.0 (#456)\n* c19309fe7ea77e44e07ce1146a655bd3a88267ab CLAUDE.md: small instruction tweaks\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v182","created_at":"2026-01-01T21:35:45Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 4413881b2d593a406021616953e46ce7b6153c9d proxy: actually add /v1/responses endpoint (#449)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v181","created_at":"2026-01-01T20:52:12Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 8df5e8563be5428dc94eae92632eab8b097f28ca proxy: add /v1/responses and /v1/audio/voices endpoints (#448)\n* 7931212d3e9660b16b66a7bd9486ebaef75c9915 proxy: add v1/images/edits API endpoint (#447)\n* 3dc36032fb21a8cfbea34b5ef94cb01029f49877 proxy: skip very slow tests in -short test mode (#446)\n* addb98646f7d945473fe4361aa56ccaa0c7fd59c proxy: add support for basic authorization (#445)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v180","created_at":"2025-12-31T05:04:58Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 37d74efc2db05805d698d1a7a06a32eeed670640 proxy: add /v1/images/generations (#443)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v179","created_at":"2025-12-28T04:18:06Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 22e098ac8b33f7c7b7711918ac976b6cb753ce9b Add Peer Model Support (#438)\n* 9864f9f517ada3c02b63ca031f1c4e741e299e25 .coderabbit.yaml: disable annoying features\n* 53b32f3601a9ef74ca1c59f46d7a1f1a0273f214 proxy: add API key support (#436)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v178","created_at":"2025-12-22T06:23:31Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 565c44766db9cdcaa0f3e61d0a60c44884b95d62 config,proxy: add new configuration logToStdout (#432)\n* e6a9e210ba769d44a04a21a96934bbe6fd233831 proxy: fix path bug in /logs/stream/{model_id} (#431)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v177","created_at":"2025-12-19T05:49:25Z","body":"## Changelog\n* d3f329f92461f3edfd69d747a8700974454bbde5 proxy: Improve logging performance and allow separate log streaming (#421)\n* 98879b38c149f253b6b520560e87dc4504b0ea3b docker: add /app to $PATH (#424)\n* 7b3b0f5eaeb60260397743f3addfb0fd5d1bbbde move header images around [skip ci]\n* 021ccceef1b18e539190057941c5b2b11e4983b7 README: update hero image\n* f03871c50a009a8ca61eb39e7f0cc2d09b1c2702 Update README.md\n* dc00d17abe6b563eadef5f9e0ea551dacb3d8395 docs: add documentation for non-root container images and security considerations (#416)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v176","created_at":"2025-11-30T07:51:20Z","body":"## Changelog\n* dea98733c30f55940d622ecf2e8085d6b8ab8477 proxy: extract metrics for v1/messages (#419)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v175","created_at":"2025-11-30T06:27:22Z","body":"## Changelog\n* bccce5fa19a30640e5d0562225a8523fd0d09e6c go.mod,ui/package-lock.json: dependency and security updates (#418)\n* c968da1b73edb4998086c2dca0d4aa2495bda839 proxy: add support for anthropic v1/messages api (#417)\n* a883d68d4ff5a37e6ec0824690f6b7116cb79ca7 feat: Add support for custom llama.cpp base image and forked llama-swap repositories (#396)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v174","created_at":"2025-11-25T18:44:13Z","body":"## Changelog\n* b1dec8b7352393ebbd39181766d1a336cd8d52c7 docker: build both root and non-root container images (#412)\n* 06523d8c1e23acbd82c62964f0b7959a75dfdb0c feat: add platform-specific process attributes support (#411)\n\n"},{"tag_name":"v173","created_at":"2025-11-17T18:43:47Z","body":"This release includes a set of quality of life features for configuring and using llama-swap: \r\n\r\n- add JSON schema for configuration file (#393) \r\n- build, commit and version information in the UI (#395)\r\n  - <img width=\"354\" height=\"239\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/84c5276a-f2ad-4ad2-916d-aaa36f96af38\" />\r\n- enable model aliases in `v1/models` (#400)\r\n- `logTimeFormat`: enable and set timestamps in log output for the proxy (#401)\r\n\r\nShout out to @ryan-steed-usa and @nint8835 for their contributions to this release. \r\n\r\n## Changelog\r\n* 86e9b93c371cdec5bc8510e423a78462125fe271 proxy,ui: add version endpoint and display version info in UI (#395)\r\n* 3acace810fc2737665059ac88ecd7dbed03dd24a proxy: add configurable logging timestamp format (#401)\r\n* 554d29e87d5611d38f3b36b30cf92201f7f7be3c feat: enhance model listing to include aliases (#400)\r\n* 3567b7df088fb392232698bdeaf2010b4e66d1fb Update image in README.md for web UI section\r\n* 38738525c9b202b44057c60c5ab09b45cbd251a5 config.example.yaml: add modeline for schema validation\r\n* c0fc85819358ad1e5ad54e866803f5e5bd8f6f6f Add configuration file JSON schema (#393)\r\n* b429349e8a3f58393bb91414e1ebb0c7258db6b2 add /ui/ to wol-proxy polling (#388)\r\n* eab2efd7b54030cf6d4a26a6fa825e91af6f8dd3 feat: improve llama.cpp base image tag for cpu (#391)\r\n* 6aedbe121a56a0562d3352c3bd343aae7b392bc0 cmd/wol-proxy: show a loading page for / (#381)\r\n* b24467ab89db285628c0baf431b113a6a603e349 fix: update containerfile user/group management commands (#379)\r\n\r\n"},{"tag_name":"v172","created_at":"2025-11-03T13:30:09Z","body":"## Changelog\n* 12b69fb718f88d6c1f085fcf58768ac928995e19 proxy: recover from panic in Process.statusUpdate (#378)\n* f91a8b2462ce4e17315a958caf9601f459070b76 refactor: update Containerfile to support non-root user execution and improve security (#368)\n\n"}]